End and cancel a lock upload under its own transaction (Sophia t295)

Sophia's export answers ResourceEnd and ResourceCancel only when they
carry the ResourceBegin's transaction; a run of this client against the
production export (Sophia fd6ea7538, which now states the rule) had its
End refused. upload_end and upload_cancel take no transaction and use the
begin's. The scripted peer refuses any other, and a mutant that sends
another is killed.

The same run then completed every exchange: negotiation with a chord,
lock fetches, a two-chunk upload, demand and permit, a presented
candidate, entry and chord events, and the republish to unlocking.
